reply.body:
I agree waiting a bit here does not concern me. But if we really try to avoid polling, it is possible to achieve so by having a `ClusterStateObserver` that triggers and blocks when the index appears. We can be sure the tasks are already registered when that happens, i.e. something like the follows

```java
final var clusterStateObserver = new ClusterStateObserver(clusterService, null, logger, new ThreadContext(Settings.EMPTY));
clusterStateObserver.waitForNextChange(new ClusterStateObserver.Listener() {
    @Override
    public void onNewClusterState(ClusterState state) {
        safeAwait(cyclicBarrier);
        safeAwait(cyclicBarrier);
    }
    ...
}, state -> state.routingTable().hasIndex(indexName));
```

